  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "The `addYears` method adds or subtracts a specified number of years to the current `NepaliDate` instance. It recalculates the underlying timestamp while retaining the month and day coordinates, adjusting the day number if the target year has fewer days in that specific month."
  }, {
    "heading": "parameters",
    "content": "| Parameter | Type     | Required | Description                                               |\n| --------- | -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `years`   | `number` | Yes      | Number of years to add (positive) or subtract (negative). |",
    "table": "table-0"
  }, {
    "heading": "return-value",
    "content": "**Type**: `NepaliDate`"
  }, {
    "heading": "return-value",
    "content": "Returns a new `NepaliDate` instance with the added or subtracted years. The original instance is not modified."
  }, {
    "heading": "exceptions",
    "content": "Throws an `Error` if the resulting year falls outside the supported Bikram Sambat calendar range (1976 BS to 2100 BS):"
  }, {
    "heading": "day-clamping-on-variable-month-lengths",
    "content": "Because month lengths in the Bikram Sambat astronomical calendar vary across years, `addYears()` automatically clamps the day component if the destination year has fewer days in that month:"
