    "heading": "astronomical-foundations--calendar-mechanics",
    "content": "Unlike the Western Gregorian calendar, which is a **solar tropical** calendar based on the cycle of the seasons (equinoxes and solstices), Bikram Sambat is a **solar sidereal (*Nirayana*)** calendar governed by the principles of classical Hindu astronomy (*Surya Siddhanta*)."
  }, {
    "heading": "1-the-sidereal-solar-year-nirayana-saur-varsha",
    "content": "A sidereal year is the time it takes the Earth to complete one full revolution around the Sun relative to the fixed stars."
  }, {
    "heading": "1-the-sidereal-solar-year-nirayana-saur-varsha",
